# Independent-review surface (R1-4, docs/dev/critical-review-2026-07-
# remediation-instructions.md §6).
#
# These paths are the trust-critical core: a defect here changes what programs
# mean, what identities attest, or what memory-safety the process has. Changes
# to them require review by someone other than the author. With branch
# protection's "require review from Code Owners" enabled, GitHub enforces that
# mechanically once a second maintainer exists.
#
# Until an independent reviewer is available, the documented fallback applies
# (remediation instructions §9 R1-4): no self-approval inside the PR that makes
# the change, and a minimum 24-hour cooling period between opening and merging
# a PR that touches any path below.

# The canonical language definition. Every implementation artifact is
# subordinate to this file, so unreviewed drift here rewrites the language.
